1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000


2
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:05,255
[rustling]

3
00:00:05,339 --> 00:00:08,091
-[moaning in distance]
-Hmm?

4
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:16,642
[Satoshi] Stink bugs, stink bugs!
That squishy white offal.

5
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:24,816
Broad beans, broad beans,
broad beans, broad beans!

6
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:28,528
-Broad beans.
-[both panting, moaning]

7
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,200
Who's a broad bean?

8
00:00:34,952 --> 00:00:36,620
I read it online.

9
00:00:37,079 --> 00:00:41,625
"When you're about to finish,
think of things you hate to last longer."

10
00:00:42,376 --> 00:00:45,379
-Then you don't have to say it out loud.
-[soft chuckle]

11
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:50,801
Chiko, how was today's?

12
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:54,429
I don't know!
How many times has this happened today?

13
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:06,775
[exclaims]

14
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:09,820
My shift got canceled today.

15
00:01:10,654 --> 00:01:12,698
[Chiko] Without it even raining?

16
00:01:13,699 --> 00:01:17,869
Yeah, it's about
the construction schedule changing.

17
00:01:17,953 --> 00:01:19,037
Mm.

18
00:01:19,121 --> 00:01:20,622
[deep inhale]

19
00:01:20,706 --> 00:01:24,459
Man, part-time jobs are so unstable.

20
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:27,004
[Chiko] Then won't you come help me out?

21
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:33,885
BIG ZAM'S
DAILY LUNCH SPECIAL

22
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:37,723
I kept you waiting.

23
00:01:41,018 --> 00:01:44,187
Presenting Mr. Karaage No. 1.

24
00:01:44,271 --> 00:01:45,981
The seasoning is a secret.

25
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:48,900
We're in the middle
of a massive karaage boom.

26
00:01:48,984 --> 00:01:51,737
No, a karaage war!

27
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:57,159
You're gonna rob every last coin
from people passing by.

28
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:58,618
Pretty genius, right?

29
00:01:58,702 --> 00:02:01,955
A karaage boom?
Talk about jumping on the bandwagon late.

30
00:02:02,039 --> 00:02:04,916
A businessman
never walks away empty-handed,

31
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,545
and an Osaka native never lets anyone
get something for free.

32
00:02:09,171 --> 00:02:13,175
You're gonna pay back the trouble
you caused your mom here.

33
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:16,845
Don't slack off, or else.

34
00:02:17,929 --> 00:02:19,723
-Got it.
-Good!

35
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:26,813
Welcome! Get your karaage here!

36
00:02:26,897 --> 00:02:30,400
Ah! "Mr. Karaage"! Branding is important.

37
00:02:30,484 --> 00:02:31,526
Got it.

38
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:32,778
[Hironi] Good! I trust you!

39
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:34,780
Right. Welcome!

40
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:37,824
Get your Mr. Karaage here!

41
00:02:37,908 --> 00:02:39,409
-Satoshi.
-Yes.

42
00:02:39,493 --> 00:02:41,828
-I'm sorry.
-[chuckles] No, not at all.

43
00:02:41,912 --> 00:02:43,121
Actually, I'm happy.

44
00:02:43,205 --> 00:02:46,083
It's been a while
since we worked together, right?

45
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,501
Here, Chiko.

46
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:51,672
Come on, you too! Say "Yes!" Ready?

47
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:55,717
Welcome! Fresh-fried karaage!

48
00:02:55,801 --> 00:02:57,094
Add "Mr."

49
00:02:57,177 --> 00:03:00,013
[both] Fresh-fried Mr. Karaage!

50
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:02,391
-Kara--
-Interested?

51
00:03:02,474 --> 00:03:04,726
[customer] One extra-large. How much?

52
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:07,896
[Satoshi] Thank you!
One extra-large. How much?

53
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:08,980
-[Chiko] Not priced.
-[Satoshi] Right.

54
00:03:09,064 --> 00:03:10,065
RED LIGHT ELEGY

55
00:03:10,649 --> 00:03:14,277
1,000 yen, 9,000 yen, full. 4,000 yen.

56
00:03:14,361 --> 00:03:15,612
EPISODE 5

57
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:18,156
Make this a weekly thing?

58
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,909
Include staff meals.

59
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:23,370
Only 500 yen each.

60
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:24,913
Wait, not on the house?

61
00:03:24,996 --> 00:03:26,915
Hironi, it's not cooked.

62
00:03:26,998 --> 00:03:28,458
[Hironi] Medium-rare!

63
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:31,128
-Hell no.
-[door opens]

64
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:33,171
-[customer] Coming in.
-Hi, welcome!

65
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,845
Chiko?

66
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:43,890
Long time no see! How have you been?

67
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:48,437
You never reach out.

68
00:03:49,104 --> 00:03:52,399
Kataoka misses you, you know.

69
00:03:52,482 --> 00:03:53,733
Who misses her?

70
00:03:53,817 --> 00:03:55,402
[Hironi] It's you, little Kataoka.

71
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:57,904
-[Chiko's friend] Cute, right?
-Shut up, idiots!

72
00:03:57,988 --> 00:04:03,118
By the way, remember
when Yusaku introduced you as his girl?

73
00:04:03,201 --> 00:04:06,455
-[Kataoka chuckles]
-He glared at me

74
00:04:06,538 --> 00:04:09,291
-right off the bat.
-[Hironi laughs]

75
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:10,792
Like this.

76
00:04:10,876 --> 00:04:13,253
Had an attitude back then.

77
00:04:14,212 --> 00:04:15,464
Speaking of that... [clears throat]

78
00:04:15,547 --> 00:04:17,382
...where's Yusaku?

79
00:04:17,466 --> 00:04:18,508
Dunno.

80
00:04:18,592 --> 00:04:22,095
[Hironi] Left his apartment. Total ghost.

81
00:04:22,471 --> 00:04:23,930
Still in Osaka?

82
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:27,476
[Hironi] Who knows.
Should show his face after prison.

83
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:29,227
[Chiko's friend] Right.

84
00:04:30,771 --> 00:04:32,022
[Kataoka sighs]

85
00:04:37,027 --> 00:04:39,738
So, you're Chiko's new guy?

86
00:04:40,322 --> 00:04:41,323
Yes.

87
00:04:42,866 --> 00:04:46,953
You look so pathetic.

88
00:04:47,746 --> 00:04:49,748
[Kataoka] Yusaku was way better.

89
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:50,874
Leave him alone.

90
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:53,710
[chuckles] Whatever, drink up!

91
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:55,462
-Wait.
-Bottoms up!

92
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:57,756
You can't drink. Don't force it.

93
00:04:57,839 --> 00:04:59,674
[Kataoka] You don't drink either?

94
00:04:59,758 --> 00:05:02,385
Such a useless punk!

95
00:05:02,469 --> 00:05:04,387
Well, cheers!

96
00:05:04,471 --> 00:05:05,931
-That's the way.
-Whoa!

97
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:10,560
-[Chiko's friends exclaiming]
-[gulping]

98
00:05:10,644 --> 00:05:11,645
It's so good!

99
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:14,397
-Hell yeah! Look at him!
-[exclaims]

100
00:05:14,481 --> 00:05:17,234
-[Kataoka] All right.
-[Hironi] Go for more.

101
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:21,571
-[chuckles]
-You look like a total idiot.

102
00:05:21,655 --> 00:05:24,950
I have to say I'm a huge dumbass!

103
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:26,201
-[smacks]
-I know, idiot.

104
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:27,452
[Satoshi gasping]

105
00:05:27,536 --> 00:05:29,871
Proud of it?

106
00:05:29,955 --> 00:05:32,791
You're just like Yusaku,

107
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:35,794
making zero cash anyway.

108
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:38,171
-Total idiot.
-[Kataoka] Yeah.

109
00:05:38,255 --> 00:05:41,675
[Chiko's friend]
He's real next-level stupid.

110
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:44,511
What are you saying?

111
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:49,224
Yusaku's a dumbass! [chuckles]

112
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:54,187
Huh? [grunts]

113
00:05:55,814 --> 00:05:58,149
[Kataoka]
What the hell do you know about him?

114
00:05:58,233 --> 00:06:00,235
[♪ tense music playing]

115
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:03,613
He's a dumbass for real,

116
00:06:04,281 --> 00:06:07,909
but he'll jump into danger for Chiko
without a second thought.

117
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:11,580
[Kataoka] You got that kind of guts?

118
00:06:11,663 --> 00:06:14,416
-Stop!
-[Chiko's friend] Relax, just watch.

119
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:18,753
I... [splutters]

120
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:22,215
Such a chicken.

121
00:06:22,549 --> 00:06:24,175
Say something!

122
00:06:24,718 --> 00:06:27,137
[grunting weakly]

123
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:30,515
[splutters] I...

124
00:06:30,599 --> 00:06:33,602
[raises voice] I'll protect Chiko!

125
00:06:33,685 --> 00:06:34,936
[♪ music fades]

126
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:44,070
[Hironi] Gosh. [chuckles]

127
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:46,990
[Kataoka laughing]

128
00:06:47,574 --> 00:06:48,909
[thuds]

129
00:06:48,992 --> 00:06:50,910
[Chiko] Satoshi! You...

130
00:06:50,994 --> 00:06:52,954
You all right?

131
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:55,582
-Get it together!
-Screw Yusaku!

132
00:06:55,665 --> 00:06:57,417
I'll take him on anytime.

133
00:06:58,084 --> 00:06:59,836
-[Kataoka] Move, Chiko.
-[Satoshi] Chiko!

134
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:02,422
[breathing heavily]

135
00:07:02,505 --> 00:07:03,506
[Satoshi gasps]

136
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:09,512
What can you do?

137
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:12,390
The best you can do

138
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:15,644
is crawl and cling to her!

139
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:19,439
Just so you know,

140
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:22,317
I'll do anything...

141
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:25,612
I'll do whatever I can
just to be with Chiko!

142
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:27,322
Will you?

143
00:07:27,405 --> 00:07:29,658
Yeah? Then prove it, you pathetic--

144
00:07:29,741 --> 00:07:31,076
[Satoshi exclaims]

145
00:07:31,159 --> 00:07:33,036
[panting]

146
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:36,665
[Kataoka groaning]

147
00:07:36,748 --> 00:07:39,834
[Chiko] Satoshi, you okay? Get up!

148
00:07:40,627 --> 00:07:43,463
[exclaims] You guys really went at it.

149
00:07:43,546 --> 00:07:44,756
[Kataoka] Shut up.

150
00:07:44,839 --> 00:07:47,842
[chuckles] Wait, you're bleeding?

151
00:07:48,218 --> 00:07:49,386
Damn it.

152
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:52,889
Hey, Chiko.

153
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:57,894
Don't you give a damn
about Yusaku anymore?

154
00:08:00,271 --> 00:08:03,066
He might be suffering out there all alone.

155
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:05,985
[♪ pensive music playing]

156
00:08:06,069 --> 00:08:07,779
I'll never forget him.

157
00:08:09,197 --> 00:08:10,198
But right now,

158
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:13,618
my only focus is this guy.

159
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:19,124
[Chiko's friend] Let's go. Get up.

160
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:22,419
[Kataoka groaning] Piece of cake, idiots.

161
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:24,254
-[Chiko's friend] You reek of puke!
-[Kataoka] Shut up!

162
00:08:26,548 --> 00:08:27,632
Sorry about that.

163
00:08:29,092 --> 00:08:31,761
I didn't mean to stir things up.

164
00:08:32,846 --> 00:08:38,309
Though, if he could pull that off sober,
I'd hand it to him.

165
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:42,647
Satoshi, let's go.

166
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:46,359
[Satoshi groans]
Chiko, my head is killing me.

167
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:50,488
Sorry for always being like this, Chiko.

168
00:08:50,572 --> 00:08:52,115
[Chiko] Yeah, I know.

169
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:55,118
[Satoshi] Stay with me forever!

170
00:08:56,161 --> 00:08:57,454
[Chiko] I'm here.

171
00:08:59,164 --> 00:09:00,331
Come back again!

172
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:10,050
[Satoshi] Oh.

173
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:13,094
Working with Mr. Inaba today
for the first time in forever.

174
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:16,389
[Chiko] Ah, Satoshi.

175
00:09:17,432 --> 00:09:19,809
This is my share of the rent
for this month.

176
00:09:19,893 --> 00:09:24,147
Huh? It's my room anyway.
You don't have to go this far.

177
00:09:24,731 --> 00:09:27,817
[Chiko] We're living together,
so paying half is only right.

178
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:32,947
-Really? Well then...
-Mm.

179
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:38,411
[Satoshi exclaims]
I'm broke again this month.

180
00:09:39,162 --> 00:09:41,122
I have to work harder.

181
00:09:41,748 --> 00:09:45,168
Just do your best.
Weren't you the "do-anything idiot"?

182
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,336
[Satoshi] Mm.

183
00:09:47,003 --> 00:09:49,464
-What?
-Tell you later.

184
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:52,342
Chiko, a goodbye kiss?

185
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:56,471
We're in public, you perverted monkey.

186
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:01,559
I guess not.

187
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:08,691
Chiko!

188
00:10:14,948 --> 00:10:17,784
[Satoshi] White 956, moving out.

189
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:19,285
[Inaba]<i> Copy.</i>

190
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:20,870
ALTERNATING ONE-WAY

191
00:10:31,798 --> 00:10:33,508
[driver] Thanks, see you later.

192
00:10:33,591 --> 00:10:36,177
-Thank you too.
-[engine revving]

193
00:10:44,519 --> 00:10:45,728
[Satoshi] Thank you for today.

194
00:10:45,812 --> 00:10:47,856
Satoshi, great work today.

195
00:10:48,606 --> 00:10:51,067
It was longer and tougher
than expected, right?

196
00:10:51,151 --> 00:10:52,152
It was.

197
00:10:52,235 --> 00:10:54,988
Well, Mr. Inaba,
I need to talk to you about something.

198
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:57,615
[Inaba] Why are you suddenly serious?

199
00:10:57,699 --> 00:10:59,701
Well, actually,

200
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:03,454
I've decided to quit this job
and start looking for a real career.

201
00:11:05,248 --> 00:11:07,500
-Really?
-Yes.

202
00:11:12,881 --> 00:11:16,134
It's not much, but happy graduation!

203
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:17,427
You didn't have to.

204
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:18,928
Thanks for everything.

205
00:11:19,304 --> 00:11:21,347
-I'm sorry.
-[can clicks, fizzes]

206
00:11:21,431 --> 00:11:22,557
Well...

207
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:23,641
Thank you.

208
00:11:23,725 --> 00:11:25,602
You're still young, Satoshi.

209
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:28,396
You have to go explore
what you're capable of.

210
00:11:28,479 --> 00:11:32,275
Well, "exploring potential"
might be a stretch.

211
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:36,154
If I'm gonna be with Chiko,
I figured I need to get my act together.

212
00:11:36,237 --> 00:11:39,199
So, get a job and maybe get married?

213
00:11:39,782 --> 00:11:42,160
Married? Us?

214
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:43,703
Of course!

215
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:45,496
A couple living together

216
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:47,165
bumping uglies night and day...

217
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:49,167
Paths like that tend to open up.

218
00:11:49,626 --> 00:11:52,337
[chuckles] Married?

219
00:11:54,464 --> 00:11:57,091
[♪ cheery music playing]

220
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:04,140
[Chiko] What's all this? What's going on?

221
00:12:04,224 --> 00:12:07,393
Well, I'm quitting my part-time job
and getting a real job!

222
00:12:07,477 --> 00:12:10,188
[Satoshi sucks teeth] All right.

223
00:12:10,271 --> 00:12:14,025
What kind of a company should I choose?

224
00:12:14,108 --> 00:12:15,610
Watch me!

225
00:12:29,582 --> 00:12:30,875
This side's done.

226
00:12:31,793 --> 00:12:33,878
Then we're done for the day.

227
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:36,381
Slow week?

228
00:12:39,384 --> 00:12:40,593
[Chiko's mom] Look at this.

229
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:51,020
Getting a new CNC lathe machine?

230
00:12:51,104 --> 00:12:52,689
It's used, though.

231
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:56,234
A tiny workshop like ours

232
00:12:56,693 --> 00:12:59,946
has to take on
the fussy jobs others reject, right?

233
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:01,447
That's it.

234
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:05,576
If we can run this through the night,
we can take on jobs we couldn't before.

235
00:13:06,661 --> 00:13:08,496
Where'd you get the money for that?

236
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:11,457
I'll scrape it together somehow.

237
00:13:12,083 --> 00:13:15,795
This is when we go on the offensive.

238
00:13:17,297 --> 00:13:19,299
Then I'll pitch in a bit more at home.

239
00:13:19,382 --> 00:13:20,508
Idiot!

240
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:22,677
I'm not gonna leech off a kid.

241
00:13:23,011 --> 00:13:24,971
Don't worry about it.

242
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:35,106
[Chiko] Got bored already?

243
00:13:36,399 --> 00:13:39,736
[Satoshi] None of these click.

244
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:43,906
I'm starting to wonder
what I'm even capable of doing.

245
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:49,037
How about this?
"Immediate hiring. Sales role."

246
00:13:50,121 --> 00:13:52,874
No way, I'm terrible at talking to people.

247
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:58,046
This one, a construction job.

248
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:03,259
Got a hernia,
and if I push it, my asthma acts up.

249
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:06,554
Bad at cooking,

250
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:08,931
and I can hardly touch a computer.

251
00:14:09,724 --> 00:14:12,143
Do you actually want a job?

252
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:14,562
Of course I do!

253
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:17,398
Then call somewhere, anywhere!

254
00:14:19,025 --> 00:14:20,359
[Satoshi] Yeah. [sighs]

255
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:23,404
[Chiko tuts]

256
00:14:24,197 --> 00:14:27,325
[Chiko breathing heavily]

257
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:30,119
-[smacks]
-[Chiko grunts angrily]

258
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,919
[Satoshi]
That's a blue-collar job magazine.

259
00:14:38,711 --> 00:14:40,463
Why are you suddenly looking too?

260
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:42,256
Not sudden at all.

261
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:44,550
I said before I wanted to be a driver.

262
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:48,679
[sighs]

263
00:14:51,057 --> 00:14:53,976
It's so good you know what you want to do.

264
00:14:55,186 --> 00:14:58,648
Something you want to do?
Don't be so spoiled.

265
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:00,108
Just do what you can.

266
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:03,861
Forgot how brutal job hunting was
back in high school?

267
00:15:06,155 --> 00:15:09,575
Back then,
I'd get nervous and get diarrhea!

268
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:12,954
But meeting Chiko changed me!

269
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:14,747
[friend] 'Cause you lost your virginity?

270
00:15:14,831 --> 00:15:18,167
-I'll fillet you like a fish.
-[groans] It's not like that!

271
00:15:19,877 --> 00:15:22,839
But if I do nothing,

272
00:15:23,339 --> 00:15:24,841
she'll leave me in the dust.

273
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:27,802
Eiji-kun, take care of this too.

274
00:15:27,885 --> 00:15:28,886
[Eiji] Sure!

275
00:15:33,099 --> 00:15:38,104
Biologically speaking, you and Chiko
are totally different species.

276
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:42,024
A garnish and a tuna steak
will never be equal anyway.

277
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:44,944
So a garnish should just accept
being thrown away?

278
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:46,529
[Eiji] Mm...

279
00:15:47,822 --> 00:15:49,031
Here, look at me.

280
00:15:49,991 --> 00:15:53,452
When I was a kid,
I didn't look up to male staff here

281
00:15:53,536 --> 00:15:55,788
and dream of working at a supermarket.

282
00:15:56,372 --> 00:15:58,916
But you have to do what you have to do.

283
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:02,753
Once you try,
you might see things differently.

284
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:07,633
Young man!

285
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:11,721
Stick a discount sticker on this too!

286
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:16,559
Can't beat these old ladies. Hang on.
Don't tell anyone, okay?

287
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:19,645
[Satoshi's mom] Fits perfectly.

288
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:22,023
Your dad would be happy too.

289
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:25,318
Too soon!
I haven't even had an interview yet.

290
00:16:25,902 --> 00:16:27,570
Stop complaining and take it.

291
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:31,115
Why do you tie like that? Let me see.

292
00:16:32,158 --> 00:16:33,159
Well...

293
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:38,247
If you don't get a proper job this time,

294
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:40,082
you're banned from this house.

295
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,836
You're gonna be an uncle soon.

296
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:45,296
Get your act together!

297
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:54,180
[Yasushi] I'll do it.

298
00:16:54,263 --> 00:16:56,140
Fold it neatly edge-to-edge.

299
00:16:56,224 --> 00:16:57,350
[Yasushi] Got it.

300
00:16:58,643 --> 00:17:00,770
[Sayaka] Redo that one.

301
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:07,902
I'm home.

302
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:12,448
Okay, goodbye.

303
00:17:15,618 --> 00:17:17,119
[Satoshi] Any luck?

304
00:17:17,203 --> 00:17:20,915
Most places require
a license held for over a year.

305
00:17:21,415 --> 00:17:22,625
I see. [sighs]

306
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:25,378
Well, I'll just keep looking
until I find one.

307
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:46,941
[Satoshi sighs]

308
00:17:57,118 --> 00:17:58,160
[phone ringing]

309
00:17:58,244 --> 00:18:00,288
Oh! It's the security company.

310
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:01,956
[breathing nervously] Huh?

311
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:05,251
Hello. What happened?

312
00:18:07,253 --> 00:18:08,296
Huh?

313
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:11,674
Chiko, Mr. Inaba collapsed!

314
00:18:12,425 --> 00:18:14,760
-[splutters] What do you mean?
-Huh?

315
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:18,639
[Satoshi]
He's now at the hospital, unconscious!

316
00:18:18,723 --> 00:18:21,976
What should I do?
If anything happens to him...

317
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:23,477
-How could I--
-Let's go.

318
00:18:37,325 --> 00:18:38,326
Come on.

319
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:05,436
[Inaba laughs]

320
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:09,774
Nah! Just malnutrition
and sleep deprivation!

321
00:19:10,191 --> 00:19:12,068
IV isn't enough,

322
00:19:12,652 --> 00:19:15,237
so I'm bingeing on everyone's gifts!

323
00:19:15,321 --> 00:19:17,156
Satoshi was crying!

324
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:18,491
I was not!

325
00:19:19,116 --> 00:19:20,743
Sorry for worrying you guys.

326
00:19:20,826 --> 00:19:23,663
But I'm glad to see both of you.

327
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:27,458
How's life?
Still going strong in both ways?

328
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:29,794
Stop talking nonsense.

329
00:19:29,877 --> 00:19:31,921
[chuckles] Right!

330
00:19:32,588 --> 00:19:36,801
Why not have a beauty here
peel an apple for me?

331
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:39,303
-Here.
-[Chiko] I'm terrible at this.

332
00:19:42,848 --> 00:19:45,351
Is this because I left?

333
00:19:45,434 --> 00:19:48,104
Did you overwork
because you were short-staffed?

334
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,563
No.

335
00:19:49,647 --> 00:19:52,066
I might not look it,
but I'm twice divorced. Mm.

336
00:19:52,692 --> 00:19:55,236
I've got plenty of red flags,
and I'm working hard

337
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:59,824
to build up my kids' savings.

338
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:03,619
That's my whatchamacallit... eye-den...

339
00:20:03,703 --> 00:20:06,997
Eye-den... tit-tee!

340
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:09,709
Maybe that's the wrong word.

341
00:20:09,792 --> 00:20:10,876
[Inaba] Is it?

342
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:15,297
Anyway, never feel guilty for no reason.

343
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:19,343
Then, until you recover, I can--

344
00:20:19,427 --> 00:20:21,762
I told you. I'm fine!

345
00:20:21,846 --> 00:20:23,973
Just do what you want, Satoshi.

346
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:27,476
If it doesn't work out,
you can always come back. Okay?

347
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:30,771
Yes.

348
00:20:40,406 --> 00:20:42,742
[grunting]

349
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:50,541
Damn! I told you I'm terrible at this!

350
00:20:50,624 --> 00:20:52,251
I didn't say a word! [chuckles]

351
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:54,044
Screw this! I'm done!

352
00:20:54,128 --> 00:20:55,755
[Inaba and Satoshi chuckle]

353
00:20:55,838 --> 00:20:59,258
-[insects chirping]
-[frog croaking]

354
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:07,558
[Satoshi] Right here?

355
00:21:08,225 --> 00:21:10,436
This is where we became one!

356
00:21:11,228 --> 00:21:12,271
It's destiny!

357
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:15,566
To be back here
on a night like this is superb!

358
00:21:16,192 --> 00:21:17,777
Yeah, I agree.

359
00:21:25,159 --> 00:21:26,160
You know,

360
00:21:27,328 --> 00:21:29,580
my dad died from overwork.

361
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:38,130
He came home, went to sleep,
and just never woke up.

362
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:41,175
[♪ gentle somber music playing]

363
00:21:47,681 --> 00:21:49,099
[groaning]

364
00:21:49,183 --> 00:21:52,353
Wh... What are you doing?

365
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:55,731
I'll do my best! I'll try everything!

366
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:02,863
If you don't get a job soon,

367
00:22:03,906 --> 00:22:05,783
I'll become a driver before you.

368
00:22:07,701 --> 00:22:09,078
[Satoshi] Wait, no!

369
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:12,164
I'm gonna find a job, work my ass off,

370
00:22:12,248 --> 00:22:14,416
and stay with you forever,

371
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:15,501
and then...

372
00:22:17,586 --> 00:22:19,922
And then what?

373
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:22,216
I will...

374
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:27,888
for now...

375
00:22:28,764 --> 00:22:30,808
be running all the way home!

376
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:33,978
-Huh? What?
-I'll start first!

377
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:39,275
[Satoshi shouts]

378
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:40,734
[grunting]

379
00:22:41,318 --> 00:22:42,403
[chuckles]

380
00:22:46,824 --> 00:22:49,326
[Satoshi shouts]

381
00:22:49,410 --> 00:22:50,411
Real idiot.

382
00:22:51,996 --> 00:22:54,206
[Satoshi shouts] I can do this!

383
00:22:56,208 --> 00:22:58,586
[Satoshi] I saw the job ad.

384
00:22:59,420 --> 00:23:02,298
Yes, my name is Yanagawa.

385
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:04,508
Right.

386
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:07,094
I'm 23.

387
00:23:07,177 --> 00:23:09,430
Moriguchi City.

388
00:23:10,014 --> 00:23:13,183
-Yes, hello?
-For now, I only have a semi license.

389
00:23:13,267 --> 00:23:15,227
-Interview? Of course.
-Yes.

390
00:23:15,311 --> 00:23:16,896
-Yes.
-Yes.

391
00:23:16,979 --> 00:23:19,732
-So, see you tomorrow.
-Then, see you tomorrow.

392
00:23:23,235 --> 00:23:24,236
Got it too?

393
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:25,613
I got an interview!

394
00:23:26,030 --> 00:23:27,114
How about you, Chiko?

395
00:23:27,573 --> 00:23:29,950
[excited gasp] It's destiny.

396
00:23:31,118 --> 00:23:33,370
-[Satoshi] Destiny!
-[Chiko] We haven't passed yet.

397
00:23:33,913 --> 00:23:34,914
Go easy on it.

398
00:23:36,707 --> 00:23:41,629
OSAKA'S TOP FOOD PICK,
KUSHIKATSU (DEEP-FRIED SKEWERS)

399
00:23:41,712 --> 00:23:43,964
[sizzling]

400
00:23:48,302 --> 00:23:49,887
[crunching]

401
00:23:52,222 --> 00:23:53,223
This is good.

402
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:56,560
[indistinct chatter]

403
00:23:59,605 --> 00:24:01,106
[Eiji] Nothing beats this place.

404
00:24:01,190 --> 00:24:02,775
MATSUI
NO DOUBLE-DIPPING

405
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:05,277
[♪ closing theme music playing]

406
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:06,277

